Review feedback addressed — 2026-06-13

Changes made to satisfy all reviewer comments:

=== Gemini comment 1: SSR safety, lifecycle cleanup, stable targeting, validation ===

1. SSR-safe GSAP plugin registration
   - Created lib/animation/scroll-trigger.ts
   - Guards gsap.registerPlugin(ScrollTrigger) behind `typeof window !== 'undefined'`
   - Follows the same pattern already established in lib/animation/flip.ts

2. React lifecycle cleanup (prevent memory leaks)
   - Created lib/animation/slide-timeline.ts (useSlideTimeline hook)
   - Uses useEffect with a cleanup callback that calls tl.kill()
   - Uses a `cancelled` flag to guard the async gsap import from acting after unmount
   - Timeline is killed on every slideIndex change AND on component unmount

3. Stable element targeting via data-anim attributes
   - Modified components/player/adjustable.tsx to render data-anim={elKey} on wrapper div
   - Every Adjustable-wrapped element (headline, supporting, points, code, quote, etc.)
     is now targetable via data-anim without fragile CSS class selectors
   - useSlideTimeline uses CSS.escape() for safe querySelector

4. lib/generation/validate.ts updated
   - Added validateTimelineEntry() helper
   - Validates at (number ≥ 0, or GSAP position string matching known patterns)
   - Validates target (non-empty string)
   - Validates tween (only whitelisted keys allowed; range checks on opacity/duration/delay/stagger)
   - Called from validateSlides() for each slide's timeline array

=== Gemini comment 2: strict tween whitelist + clarify at field semantics ===

5. TimelineTween strictly whitelisted (core/schemas/types.ts)
   - Only: opacity, x, y, xPercent, yPercent, scale, scaleX, scaleY, rotation,
           duration, ease, stagger, delay
   - Excludes: width/height, left/top/right/bottom, margin/padding, color, zIndex,
               innerHTML/textContent, attr, and all other arbitrary properties

6. TimelineEntry.at documented with both absolute and relative offset semantics:
   - number → absolute seconds from timeline start (e.g. 0, 0.3, 1.5)
   - string → GSAP position parameter:
       "<"       align with start of previous tween
       ">"       end of previous tween (default GSAP behaviour)
       "+=0.2"   0.2s after end of previous
       "-=0.1"   0.1s before end of previous (overlap)
       "<+=0.3"  0.3s after start of previous

